-- ===== 5) 听力 6篇/30题(audio_url 待 TTS) =====
DELETE FROM public.junior_listening_exercises WHERE volume='required1' AND unit='U4';
Reporter: A strong earthquake hit the city early this morning.
Anchor: Do we know the magnitude?
Reporter: Yes, it reached a magnitude of seven point eight.
Anchor: How are the rescue teams doing?
Reporter: Soldiers and doctors are digging out people who are trapped.
Anchor: What do the survivors need most?
Reporter: They need clean water, food and shelter right now.', '主播连线灾区记者;记者说今早一场强震袭击城市;震级7.8;救援队中士兵和医生正挖出被困者;幸存者最需要的是干净的水、食物和避难所。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"When did the earthquake hit the city?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Early this morning.","Late last night.","Yesterday afternoon.","A week ago."]},{"q":"What was the magnitude of the quake?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Eight point seven.","Seven point eight.","Five point eight.","Six point five."]},{"q":"Who are digging out the trapped people?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Soldiers and doctors.","Tourists.","Shop workers.","Teachers."]},{"q":"What do the survivors need most right now?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Books and toys.","Water, food and shelter.","New phones.","More reporters."]},{"q":"Where is the reporter speaking from?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["A library.","A train station.","Near the disaster area.","A shopping mall."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required1', 'U4');
In less than a minute, a large city lay in ruins.
But hope was not lost after the quake.
Soldiers, doctors and workers came from all over the country to help.
With great effort, a new Tangshan was built upon the ruins.', '1976年一场致命地震几乎摧毁了整个唐山;不到一分钟,大城市成了废墟;但震后希望未灭;来自全国的士兵、医生和工人前来帮忙;凭着巨大努力,一座新唐山在废墟上建起。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What happened to Tangshan in 1976?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["A flood covered it.","A typhoon hit it.","Nothing serious happened.","A deadly earthquake destroyed most of it."]},{"q":"How fast did the city fall into ruins?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["In less than a minute.","Over many years.","In about a week.","It never fell."]},{"q":"What does the passage say about hope after the quake?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["It was completely lost.","It was not lost.","No one cared.","It came too late."]},{"q":"Who came to help the city?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Only the local people.","No one at all.","Soldiers, doctors and workers from all over the country.","Foreign tourists."]},{"q":"What was finally built upon the ruins?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["A small village.","An empty field.","A shopping centre only.","A new Tangshan."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required1', 'U4');
Mrs Fors: First, enough water and food for three days.
Student: What about when the power goes out?
Mrs Fors: Keep a flashlight and a radio so you can hear the news.
Student: Should we have anything for injuries?
Mrs Fors: Yes, always keep a first aid kit on hand.
Student: And if we are trapped after a quake?
Mrs Fors: Tap on a pipe or use a whistle so we can find you.', '学生问 Fors 女士应急包里放什么;先是三天的水和食物;停电时备手电和收音机听新闻;受伤要备急救箱;若被困,敲管子或吹哨子好让人找到你。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"How much water and food should a kit hold?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Enough for three days.","Enough for one hour.","Enough for a month.","None at all."]},{"q":"Why keep a flashlight and a radio?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["To play games.","For when the power goes out and to hear the news.","To sell them later.","To give to friends."]},{"q":"What should you keep for injuries?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["A camera.","A football.","A first aid kit.","A map."]},{"q":"What should a trapped person do?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Shout for hours.","Run around.","Stay completely silent.","Tap on a pipe or use a whistle."]},{"q":"Who is giving the advice?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Mrs Fors.","A shop owner.","A bus driver.","A tourist."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required1', 'U4');
Remember three words: drop, cover and hold on.
Get under a strong table and protect your head.
If you are outdoors, move to an open space away from buildings.
Most importantly, try to stay calm during the shaking.', '若室内地震,别立刻往外跑;记住三个词:伏地、遮挡、稳住;躲到结实的桌子下并护住头;若在室外,到远离建筑的开阔地;最重要的是摇晃时保持镇静。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What should you NOT do if a quake happens indoors?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Protect your head.","Run outside at once.","Get under a table.","Stay calm."]},{"q":"What three words should you remember?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Run, jump and shout.","Look, listen and wait.","Drop, cover and hold on.","Eat, drink and sleep."]},{"q":"Where should you go if you are outdoors?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Into the nearest building.","Under a tall wall.","Onto a bridge.","An open space away from buildings."]},{"q":"What should you protect when under a table?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Your head.","Your phone.","Your bag.","Your shoes."]},{"q":"What is the most important thing during the shaking?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["To take photos.","To stay calm.","To make phone calls.","To find your friends."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required1', 'U4');
Woman: I was in shock. Everything happened so fast.
Reporter: How did you escape from your home?
Woman: I ran out before the walls fell down.
Reporter: How were you finally rescued?
Woman: A rescue worker heard me tapping on a pipe.
Reporter: What do you want to say to those who helped?
Woman: I will always be grateful to them for saving my life.', '记者问女幸存者那晚的感受;她说很震惊,一切发生得太快;她在墙塌前跑了出来;后来救援人员听见她敲管子的声音;她对救命之人永远感激。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"How did the woman feel that night?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["She was bored.","She was sleepy.","She was in shock.","She was happy."]},{"q":"How did she escape from her home?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["She stayed in bed.","She climbed onto the roof.","She drove away.","She ran out before the walls fell."]},{"q":"How was she finally rescued?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["A worker heard her tapping on a pipe.","She walked out alone.","A dog carried her out.","She called on the phone."]},{"q":"What does she feel towards those who helped?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Anger.","Gratitude.","Fear.","Surprise."]},{"q":"Who is asking the questions?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["A doctor.","A teacher.","A reporter.","A soldier."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required1', 'U4');
Before any disaster, make a family safety plan.
Decide where to meet if you are not together.
Keep an emergency kit ready at home.
A little preparation today can make a big difference tomorrow.', '一个也许能救命的小贴士:任何灾难前,做一个家庭安全计划;约好走散后在哪会合;在家备好应急包;今天的一点准备,明天会有大不同。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is the tip mainly about?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Buying a new house.","Going on holiday.","Cooking meals.","Making a family safety plan."]},{"q":"What should a family decide in advance?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Where to meet if not together.","What films to watch.","Which shop to visit.","What clothes to wear."]},{"q":"What should be kept ready at home?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["A football.","An emergency kit.","A new car.","A photo album."]},{"q":"When should you make these preparations?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["During the disaster.","After the disaster.","Before any disaster.","Never."]},{"q":"What can a little preparation today do?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Waste your time.","Cost a lot of money.","Make people worried.","Make a big difference tomorrow."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required1', 'U4');

-- ===== 6) 写作 1篇(旅行邮件) =====
DELETE FROM public.junior_writing_prompts WHERE volume='required1' AND unit='U4';
【新闻大意】2004年12月26日,印度尼西亚附近海域发生9.0级强烈地震,引发横扫亚洲海岸的海啸,逾6500人遇难、上百万人受灾;多国组织救援,但道路损毁使物资运送困难。', 'Suppose you are Li Hua. Write a summary (about 80 words) of the news below, including: 1) when and where the disaster happened and what it was; 2) the main effects (deaths / damage); 3) the rescue and aid. A summary keeps only the main points—do not copy sentences, add details or give personal opinions.', '["时间地点+灾难(On 26 December 2004, a powerful earthquake off Indonesia caused a tsunami…)","主要影响(More than 6,500 people were killed and over a million were affected…)","救援与援助(Foreign aid was organised, but damaged roads made delivery difficult…)","只写主要信息、转述不照抄、不加评论"]'::jsonb, 70, 100, 'On 26 December 2004, a powerful earthquake struck under the sea near Indonesia and caused a huge tsunami that crashed into coastlines across Asia. More than 6,500 people were killed and over a million more were affected, as homes, cars and whole villages were swept away. Foreign aid was quickly organised for the affected countries. However, dangerous conditions and damaged roads made it very hard to deliver food and supplies to the survivors.', '【15 分制】A 档(13-15):五要素齐全、组织有条理、语言准确多样;B 档(10-12):要点较全、少量错误;C 档(7-9):要点偏少、句型简单;D 档(0-6):内容不完整、错误多。', '["A powerful earthquake struck under the sea and caused a huge tsunami.","More than 6,500 people were killed and over a million more were affected.","Foreign aid was organised, but damaged roads made it hard to deliver supplies."]'::jsonb, '[{"wrong":"The earthquake happened in 26 December 2004.","correct":"The earthquake happened on 26 December 2004.","note":"具体某天用 on,不用 in。"},{"wrong":"More than 6,500 people killed.","correct":"More than 6,500 people were killed.","note":"被动语态需要 be + 过去分词 were killed。"},{"wrong":"Damaged roads made hard to deliver food.","correct":"Damaged roads made it hard to deliver food.","note":"make it + adj + to do,形式宾语 it 不可省。"}]'::jsonb, '【摘要结构】
第1句 时间地点+灾难:On … , a … earthquake … caused a tsunami …
第2句 主要影响:More than … were killed and … were affected …
第3句 救援援助:Foreign aid was organised, but … made it hard to deliver …', 2, 'required1', 'U4');

